Three-domain synthetic POC - LIVE run over real cross-host TLS (VL-096 live)
============================================================================

AUTHOR-EXECUTED on the real VirtualBox deployment. Recorded by Claude from the
author's pasted runner output. Referent: the three generated reports
EVIDENCE/proofs/three_domain_poc/reports/{medical,legal,finance}_report.md
(Mode: live; generated 2026-06-10).

Surface
-------
- gate:       VM-A  https://192.168.56.101:8000        (pep, signs every ELIGIBLE)
- target:     VM-B  https://192.168.56.102:9000/target (reference enforcing target, SIGNED-mode)
- publisher:  VM-B  https://192.168.56.102:9100        (signs the published record live)
- client:     Windows laptop (host-only net), driving poc_runner.py --mode live
- TLS:        dev CA (deploy/tls/certs/ca.crt), client verifies via requests(verify=ca)
- gate decision window: 300s (default), so the timing-only stale_decision case was
  SKIPPED (it is proven deterministically in the in-process report); every other
  case ran over real transport.

Per-domain: the domain manifest (med-1.0 / legal-1.0 / fin-1.0) was pinned onto
MANIFEST/manifest.json on BOTH hosts and the gate + publisher rebuilt, so the gate's
on-disk manifest, the publisher's signed-record manifest_sha256, and the client's
interaction pins all matched (three-way) for that domain's run.

